maya: Quick PR #4680 to tighten streaming & pagination snippets across py/ts/go. Goal: show stateless resume, periodic checkpoint (save every N), and a minimal retry wrapper. PTAL.
eli: Love the direction. Add a one-liner that tokens are opaque and not sequential.
qi: Agree. Also add an idempotency note under retries: prefer idempotent ops when replaying.
tom: TS retry helper I'll propose:
```ts
async function retry(fn){
  for(let i=0;i<3;i++){
    try{return await fn()}
    catch(e){if(i===2)throw e;await new Promise(r=>setTimeout(r,100*(2**i)))}
  }
}
```
Use `retry(()=>client.stream(...))`.
eli: For Python show periodic checkpointing, e.g.
```py
with client.stream(cid, resume_token=tok) as s:
  for i,ch in enumerate(s):
    handle(ch)
    if i%10==0: save(tok:=ch.resume_token)
```
qi: Go can be a one-liner pattern: open stream, loop, write token on shutdown. Keep tiny.
